WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.443
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.743 --> 00:00:09.350
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:16.203
Unit six: Mixed Conditionals. Today you will combine past and present time in conditional sentences.

4
00:00:16.503 --> 00:00:19.016
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:23.037
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:25.186
Past condition.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:29.367
Past condition means the if-part refers to the past.

8
00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:31.460
If I had studied...

9
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.132
Your turn. Say: Past condition.

10
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:39.200
Past condition.

11
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.067
Present result.

12
00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:44.512
Present result means the result is in the present.

13
00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:46.617
...I would be a doctor now.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:49.823
Your turn. Say: Present result.

15
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.842
Present result.

16
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.782
Present condition.

17
00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.141
Present condition means the if-part describes a present state.

18
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.332
If I were more confident...

19
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:05.801
Your turn. Say: Present condition.

20
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:09.865
Present condition.

21
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:11.757
Past result.

22
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.446
Past result means the result was in the past.

23
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.295
...I would have applied.

24
00:01:17.883 --> 00:01:20.768
Your turn. Say: Past result.

25
00:01:23.633 --> 00:01:24.809
Past result.

26
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:26.679
Mixed time.

27
00:01:27.683 --> 00:01:30.136
Mixed time means two different time frames.

28
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.192
This is mixed time.

29
00:01:32.783 --> 00:01:35.389
Your turn. Say: Mixed time.

30
00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:39.339
Mixed time.

31
00:01:40.083 --> 00:01:41.038
Combine.

32
00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.945
Combine means to join together.

33
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.946
Combine the clauses.

34
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.900
Your turn. Say: Combine.

35
00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:52.652
Combine.

36
00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:54.418
Complex.

37
00:01:55.417 --> 00:01:57.532
Complex means made of many parts.

38
00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.907
A complex structure.

39
00:02:00.517 --> 00:02:03.041
Your turn. Say: Complex.

40
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.052
Complex.

41
00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:08.783
Nuance.

42
00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:12.050
Nuance means a small difference in meaning.

43
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.046
A subtle nuance.

44
00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.535
Your turn. Say: Nuance.

45
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.389
Nuance.

46
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.874
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:29.610
Visal, how does the past change your life today?

48
00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:41.415
If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now. This mixed conditional links a past condition to a present result: if + past perfect, would + base verb.

49
00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:43.820
What is the other pattern?

50
00:02:44.917 --> 00:02:56.204
If + past simple, would have + past participle links a present condition to a past result: If I were more confident, I would have applied for the job last year.

51
00:02:57.317 --> 00:02:58.236
Why use them?

52
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:11.720
They express nuance, because the time of the condition and the time of the result are different. Use the third conditional when both are past, the second when both are present or future.

53
00:03:12.867 --> 00:03:14.367
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.217 --> 00:03:19.956
Grammar focus: Mixed conditionals: past to present, present to past.

55
00:03:20.256 --> 00:03:21.327
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.017 --> 00:03:24.806
If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.

57
00:03:25.717 --> 00:03:28.599
If I were more confident, I would have applied last year.

58
00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:32.655
If she had saved money, she could buy a house today.

59
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:44.925
Past condition → present result: if + past perfect, would + base verb. Present condition → past result: if + past simple, would have + past participle.

60
00:03:45.683 --> 00:03:49.357
Be careful! Don't say: If I studied, I would be a doctor.

61
00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.426
Say: If I had studied, I would be a doctor now.

62
00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:56.470
Use a past condition.

63
00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:59.919
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:02.071
Past Meets Present.

65
00:04:02.371 --> 00:04:05.566
If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.

66
00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:09.797
If I were more confident, I would have asked for the job.

67
00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.529
The nuance is that the condition and the result belong to different times.

68
00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:18.613
If she had saved money, she could buy a house today.

69
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.993
Mixed conditionals are complex, but they add precision.

70
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.171
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:29.017 --> 00:04:31.446
If I had left earlier, I blank here now.

72
00:04:31.746 --> 00:04:35.155
A, would be. B, would have been. C, will be.

73
00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.491
The answer is A: would be.

74
00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:43.986
If I blank braver, I would have spoken.

75
00:04:44.286 --> 00:04:47.255
A, am. B, were. C, had been.

76
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.254
The answer is B: were.

77
00:04:53.417 --> 00:04:57.448
Which time frames does 'If I had studied, I'd be a doctor now' mix?

78
00:04:57.748 --> 00:05:03.665
A, past → present. B, present → past. C, future → past.

79
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.152
The answer is A: past → present.

80
00:05:11.317 --> 00:05:12.585
Which is correct?

81
00:05:12.885 --> 00:05:21.972
A, If I had known, I'd tell you now.. B, If I had known, I would have told you.. C, If I knew, I would have told you yesterday..

82
00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:28.624
The answer is B: If I had known, I would have told you..

83
00:05:29.783 --> 00:05:32.120
According to the reading, what can she buy?

84
00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:35.760
A, a house. B, a car. C, a boat.

85
00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.009
The answer is A: a house.

86
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.352
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:46.217 --> 00:05:48.832
Try writing your own mixed conditional sentence.

88
00:05:57.617 --> 00:05:59.221
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:59.521 --> 00:06:12.927
If I had moved to the city five years ago, I would have better job opportunities now. I stayed in my village, so my career is different today. This is a mixed conditional because the past condition has a present result.

90
00:06:13.227 --> 00:06:14.786
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:15.683 --> 00:06:22.248
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and mixed conditionals: past to present, present to past.

92
00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:27.766
Today's value is reflective awareness. Notice your own experience with care and honesty.

93
00:06:28.066 --> 00:06:30.719
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:31.019 --> 00:06:33.717
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

